# The scaffold templates are compiled into the binary with `include_str!`, so
# their bytes on disk are the bytes a new loop gets. A Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise hand every `.sh` launcher CRLF endings,
# which POSIX sh reads as part of each command. The `.cmd` templates are LF
# here too; `scaffold::crlf` converts them on the way out.
runtime/crates/loopsmith-cli/templates/** text eol=lf
